Feature: store-module

Affected projects:
- Libraries/vUX: new Store module (vUX-store.js), shared state for the parts of a page that show
  the same data. A store holds one flat object of declared fields (set() refuses unknown names),
  optional computed fields (config.computed, fixed at initialize()), field-level subscriptions
  (subscribe(fn, fields) -> unsubscribe), batch() for one announcement over several sets, reset(),
  and bind()/bindList() that drive Component instances, DataViews and keyed Component lists. Changes
  are compared with Object.is and announced synchronously; a subscriber's own set() is queued for a
  second round so every subscriber in a round sees the same state; 100 rounds is the loop limit; a
  failing subscriber does not stop the others and the first error is rethrown.
  Component and DataView gain a read-only 'destroyed' property so a binding on a destroyed target
  drops itself. Guide doc/store.md, example examples/store/, module registry entry.
  Version bump v4.0.0 -> v4.1.0 (minor: new module): core file renamed src/vUX-core-4.1.0.js and
  every import, header, doc and example label follows. dist/4.1.0/ is not built yet (./minify.sh,
  at release time).
- Workspace .version: Libraries/vUX=v4.1.0 (minor over the last tag v4.0.0).

Consumer impact: additive. Pages that import src/vUX-core-4.0.0.js directly must use
src/vUX-core-4.1.0.js (none in Apps/ do; they import component modules through lib/vUX).

Verified: a headless-Chrome test page ran 38 checks on the module (notification rules, batch,
re-entrancy, loop guard, computed atomicity, reset, bind/bindList/DataView, teardown, errors), all
passing; the example page was driven end to end with no page errors and screenshotted at 1280px
and 390px.

Validation: features-validator verdict PASS WITH FINDINGS (no Critical/High). All findings fixed:
first bind apply runs as a round, bindings get the round's state, batch drops set-back fields,
computed functions get their own copy, '__proto__' refused, persistence doc pattern corrected,
stale variable removed, isPlainObject proposed as a core utility (potentialUtilities.md #11).
